]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Format"] [:td {:colspan "2"} "Each athlete competed in the long jump, shot put, and 100 yard dash as part of the overall combined exercises. Scoring was basically from 0-10 for each of the three events. In the long jump, 18 feet earned 10 points, and 1/10th point was added or subtracted for each 1/10th foot short of or beyond 18 feet. In the shot put, 30 feet () earned 10 points, and 1/10th point was added or subtracted for each 1/5th foot short of or beyond 30 feet. In the 100 yard dash, 11.0 seconds earned 10 points, and « point was added for subtracted for each 1/5th second faster or slower than 11.0 seconds."]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "This event was an offshoot of the " [:a {:href "/results/70009"} "individual all-around for apparatus and field sports"] ", with the scores in the three track &amp; field events (100 yards, long jump, shot put) used to determine placements. The event could really be considered a track &amp; field multi-event, sort of an early triathlon, and it could be included within the track &amp; field events. Scoring was on a 0-10 scale, but athletes could score more than the maximum in all three events."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Unlike the combined all-around and " [:a {:href "/results/70016"} "all-around for apparatus work"] ", which were dominated by German-speaking gymnasts, the Americans were pre-eminent in the field sports, taking the top six places, and 18 of the top 20. The title went to Indianapolis’ " [:a {:href "/athletes/78371"} "Max Emmerich"] ", who scored well over the maximum, with 35.7 points."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Points"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/78371"} "Max Emmerich"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1